TABLE:

Table are used to represent the real life table data.

syntax:

<table>
    <caption>Table caption or title </caption>
    <tr>
        <th>header1</th>
        <th>header2</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>data1</td>
        <td>data2</td>
    </tr>

</table>

<tr> -->used to display table row
<td> -->used to display table data
<th> -->used to display table header

SEMANTIC TAG IN HTML:

<tbody> --> to wrap table header
<thead> --> to wrap table head
<tfoot> --> to wrap table foot 

COLSPAN & ROWSPAN ATTRIBUTES:

        span --> Area Covered by a cell.
used to create cells which spans over multiple rows or columns
        Rowspan = "(num of Rows to cover single header) " 
        Colspan = " (num of columns to cover single header)"

FORMS IN HTML:

Forms are used to collect the information from user.

Syntax:

<form>
        Form Content
</form>

ACTION ATTRIBUTE:

Action attributes is used to define what action needs to performed 
when a form is submitted or where the form data should be sent.

<form action="/action.php">
<form action="/action">

FORM ELEMENTS:

input
->used to create multiple form controls.
->there are multiple types of inputs that can be created using type attribute.

type attribute:
<input>
<input type="text">
<input type="password">
<input type="number">
<input type="time">
<input type="color">
<input type="date">
<input type="email">

.placeholder attribute
syntax:
    <input type="text" placeholder="Enter Name">

label :
->Label element represents a caption for an item in a user interface.

syntax:

<label>
    Enter your username:
    <input type="text" placeholder="username">
</label>

label classical Approach

<label for="username">Enter your name:</label>
<input type="text" id="username" placeholder="username">

#BUTTON ELEMENT:
<button>submit</button>

*type attribute:
<button type="submit">submit</button>
<button type="reset">do something</button>
<button type="button">do something</button>

#INPUT ELEMENT:
Button using input

<input type="submit">
<input type="submit" value="Click Me">

#NAME ATTRIBUTES:

Name of the form control.Submitted with the form as part of 
Name/value pair.

synyax:
<input type="text" placeholder="enter username" id="username" name="username"/>

CHECKBOX:
 when we group the different option then also can   check multiple box at a time 
<input type="checkbox" id="age" name="age" checked/> (it already checked )
<label for="age">I am 18+</label>

RADIO BUTTON:

when we group then different radiio button can't check once we can  not  check multiple box at a time.
<input type="radio" name="fruit" id="apple" value="apple" />
<lable for="apple">Apple</label>

#SELECT ELEMENT:
Dropdown

<select id="profession" name="profession">
    <option selected>Choose your option</option>
    <option value="stud">Student</option>
    <option value="dev">Developer</option>
</select>

#INPUT ELEMENT:
Range:

syntax:
<label for="volu">Select volume range</label>
<input type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50" step="10" name="vol" id="volu" >

#TEXT AREA:

<label for="feedback">Please provide your valuable feedback:</label>
<textarea id="feedback"></textarea>